# The Paddle MCP servers authenticate with OAuth — no API keys required.
#
# The first time your agent uses paddle-sandbox or paddle-live, it opens a
# browser to authorize with Paddle. There are no MCP environment variables to
# set here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: authenticate with an API key instead of OAuth
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you'd rather use a Paddle API key, add an Authorization header to the
# paddle-sandbox / paddle-live entries in your plugin's MCP config, e.g.:
#
#   "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY}" }
#
# then export the matching key(s) in the shell that launches your editor.
# Generate keys at Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication:
#   - Live:    https://vendors.paddle.com/authentication-v2
#   - Sandbox: https://sandbox-vendors.paddle.com/authentication-v2  (pdl_sdbx_ prefix)
#
# export PADDLE_LIVE_API_KEY=
# export PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
#
# Note: some skills generate server-side code for *your app* that uses the
# Paddle SDK with a PADDLE_API_KEY. That's a separate credential you set
# in your own project's environment — not here.
